 record with\n  defined pass/fail criteria against the agreed thresholds.\n- Given the collected parity data, when the campaign concludes, then a\n  go/no-go recommendation with a cleared-model list is published, measured by\n  a report accepted by the strategy stakeholders.\n- Given the campaign findings, when ROCm-specific constraints are found\n  (driver prerequisites, image versions, model-specific failures), then they\n  are documented for the productization and documentation work that follows.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n  establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30607,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-995343cca3aa05ea","agent_id":"a359e5adee496fd47","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"ae43b6b5-a60b-43b5-9055-0b87f187e79b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:35:30.574Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
