n- Given the PyTorch ROCm worker images, when used per documentation, then the\n  pinned image references are recorded for release, measured by the release\n  manifest.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Requires physical AMD Instinct hardware for validation; access is\n  unresolved at strategy level (procurement or partner lab).\n- Upstream PyTorch/ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and upstream\n  communities.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32557,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-995343cca3aa05ea","agent_id":"a359e5adee496fd47","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"d3b233eb-2540-497c-9533-a29793f39aeb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:36:01.428Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
