{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4940ece1-8b12-4caf-a6f4-a64c0f8efa67","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf8ec4dbc5ad997f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-94fau4p7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E005.md","content":"# Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu resources\n\n## Description\n\nExtend the Distributed Workloads queueing layer so that AMD GPU resources\n(amd.com/gpu) are handled in Kueue quota and admission. Today GPU quota\nhandling covers NVIDIA resources; AMD Instinct nodes expose amd.com/gpu, and\njobs requesting them must be admitted with correct quota accounting and gang\nsemantics (all-or-nothing admission via waitForPodsReady).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define/configure the Kueue resource flavor and ClusterQueue/LocalQueue\n  quota model for amd.com/gpu resources on AMD Instinct node pools.\n- Ensure admission of multi-pod distributed jobs requesting amd.com/gpu\n  preserves gang semantics (no partial admission of a job's pods).\n- Validate quota accounting and queueing behavior for jobs requesting\n  amd.com/gpu on physical AMD Instinct hardware (hardware access is a shared\n  precondition with the serving validation campaign).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a ClusterQueue with an amd.com/gpu flavor, when a workload requests\n  amd.com/gpu resources, then quota is accounted against the flavor and\n  admission respects the configured quota, measured by Kueue workload\n  admission state and quota usage.\n- Given a distributed multi-pod workload requesting amd.com/gpu, when the\n  full request cannot be met, then the workload remains pending without\n  partial pod admission (gang semantics), measured by Kueue admission\n  behavior and pending-workload metrics.\n- Given queues configured for AMD GPU pools, when training workloads are\n  submitted, then they queue and are admitted in order with correct quota\n  handling, measured by Kueue pending/admitted workload metrics.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Requires physical AMD Instinct hardware for end-to-end validation; access\n  is unresolved at strategy level (procurement or partner lab).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32557,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-995343cca3aa05ea","agent_id":"a359e5adee496fd47","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"a1096977-4cea-4c48-9de5-008b4b4335ee","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:36:10.094Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
