{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b099facf550e7033","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM serving parity\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 0\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM serving parity\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tRun a validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct accelerator nodes to\n30\testablish first-hand functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving\n31\tof the platform's supported model set on ROCm. The campaign produces the\n32\tgo/no-go recommendation and the cleared-model list that scopes productization\n33\tof a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime. This resolves the strategy's central\n34\tunknown: upstream vLLM publishes ROCm support, but the platform has no\n35\tfirst-hand parity data for its supported models.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Secure access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes (procurement or partner-lab\n40\t  access — currently unresolved; this is a precondition for campaign start).\n41\t- Define the functional and performance parity criteria and thresholds for\n42\t  the go/no-go decision (the strategy does not state quantitative thresholds).\n43\t- For each model in the supported model set, run vLLM serving on ROCm using\n44\t  upstream ROCm runtime images and record:\n45\t  - functional correctness of serving (successful loads, inference outputs);\n46\t  - performance measurements relative to the comparable CUDA baseline.\n47\t- Produce a go/no-go report per model with a recommended productization scope\n48\t  (the cleared-model list) and any remediation findings (driver versions,\n49\t  image versions, known ROCm issues encountered).\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given access to physical AMD Instinct nodes, when the supported model set\n54\t  is served with vLLM on ROCm, then functional and performance parity data\n55\t  exists for every model in the set, measured by a per-model test record with\n56\t  defined pass/fail criteria against the agreed thresholds.\n57\t- Given the collected parity data, when the campaign concludes, then a\n58\t  go/no-go recommendation with a cleared-model list is published, measured by\n59\t  a report accepted by the strategy stakeholders.\n60\t- Given the campaign findings, when ROCm-specific constraints are found\n61\t  (driver prerequisites, image versions, model-specific failures), then they\n62\t  are documented for the productization and documentation work that follows.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n67\t  establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n68\t  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-843dea58d8e936e4","agent_id":"ac39359585d532d5a","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"c626027f-a458-4470-98cb-0bc08e3bd7f4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:38:56.446Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b099facf550e7033","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
