{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ebd20c3581aeeb7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: Scope is rewritten to the model subset cleared by the validation\n15\t    campaign; on a full no-go the productization work is removed.\n16\tai_signals:\n17\t  change_specificity: 0\n18\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n19\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n20\t  existing_foundation: 1\n21\t  open_questions: -1\n22\t  external_dependency: -1\n23\t  human_process_gates: 0\n24\t  repo_access: 1\n25\t  architecture_claims: 1\n26\timplementation_type: null\n27\tinvestigation_signals: null\n28\tai_implementability: Medium\n29\tai_implementability_score: 2\n30\tjira_key: null\n31\tbranch: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tProductize a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models cleared by\n38\tthe AMD Instinct validation campaign, so that RHOAI can serve those models on\n39\tAMD accelerators. Today only CUDA (NVIDIA) runtime builds are productized;\n40\tupstream vLLM publishes ROCm builds that are not shipped or supported. This\n41\tepic turns the validated subset into a productized runtime.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Build and release a vLLM ROCm serving runtime image from the existing\n46\t  midstream vLLM repos, for the model set cleared by the validation campaign.\n47\t- Pin the image to an upstream ROCm runtime release aligned with the platform\n48\t  release train (upstream cadence is AMD/community-controlled; tracking and\n49\t  digest pinning is part of this scope).\n50\t- Provide the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime templates that expose the\n51\t  ROCm runtime for AMD Instinct nodes, requesting amd.com/gpu resources.\n52\t- Validate that KServe InferenceServices using the ROCm serving runtime\n53\t  schedule and serve correctly on AMD Instinct nodes (KServe itself requires\n54\t  no code changes — this is the passive-component validation).\n55\t- Ensure the build pipeline for the ROCm image variant is green through the\n56\t  onboarded Konflux setup (the pipeline onboarding runs in parallel; its\n57\t  first green execution gates release, not development).\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given the cleared-model list from the validation campaign, when the ROCm\n62\t  serving runtime is productized, then every cleared model serves\n63\t  successfully on AMD Instinct nodes via KServe InferenceServices, measured\n64\t  by end-to-end serving tests per cleared model.\n65\t- Given the ROCm runtime image, when it is released, then the image digest is\n66\t  pinned to an upstream ROCm release compatible with the platform release\n67\t  train, measured by the release manifest.\n68\t- Given an InferenceService selecting the ROCm serving runtime, when deployed\n69\t  to a node pool with AMD Instinct accelerators, then pods schedule with\n70\t  amd.com/gpu resources and become Ready, measured by InferenceService status\n71\t  conditions.\n72\t- Given the Konflux build pipeline for the ROCm image variant, when a change\n73\t  lands, then the pipeline builds the image green, measured by a passing\n74\t  Konflux build for the runtime image.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n79\t  models the validation campaign clears.\n80\t\n81\t## Risks\n82\t\n83\t- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n84\t  communities and may not align with platform release trains.\n85\t- Full no-go from the validation campaign removes this epic; a partial\n86\t  cleared-model list rewrites its scope.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-843dea58d8e936e4","agent_id":"ac39359585d532d5a","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"daa43139-fc47-4f36-a12d-357176ad6f53","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:38:57.417Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ebd20c3581aeeb7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
