{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0597d122345feca","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: Konflux build pipeline for the vLLM ROCm serving image\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: konflux-onboarding\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the validation campaign no-goes, no ROCm image is productized\n16\t    and the dedicated build pipeline is not needed.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\tinvestigation_signals: null\n28\tai_implementability: High\n29\tai_implementability_score: 6\n30\tjira_key: null\n31\tbranch: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Konflux build pipeline for the vLLM ROCm serving image\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tOnboard the build pipeline for the new vLLM ROCm serving runtime image\n38\tvariant into Konflux. The vLLM midstream repos are already Konflux-onboarded\n39\tfor existing (CUDA) builds; this epic adds the build configuration for the\n40\tROCm image variant so it can be built and released through the standard\n41\tplatform pipeline. This is a new container image in an existing repo, so no\n42\trepo onboarding is needed — pipeline onboarding starts immediately and runs\n43\tin parallel with the runtime image implementation work.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Add Konflux build configuration (image variant, build recipe) for the vLLM\n48\t  ROCm serving runtime image in the existing onboarded repos.\n49\t- Wire the new image variant into the existing release pipeline so it is\n50\t  built and published per platform version alongside the CUDA builds.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given the Konflux configuration for the ROCm image variant, when a build\n55\t  is triggered, then the image builds green through Konflux, measured by a\n56\t  passing pipeline run producing the ROCm runtime image.\n57\t- Given the release pipeline, when a platform version is cut, then the ROCm\n58\t  image variant is built and published through the same mechanism as the\n59\t  existing runtime builds, measured by the released image artifact.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n64\t  models the validation campaign clears (build-pipeline enablement).\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-843dea58d8e936e4","agent_id":"ac39359585d532d5a","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"0eb9920e-6be6-4d59-b731-b6bd4762567f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:38:58.423Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0597d122345feca","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
