{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af8527b7064ee1ca","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n3\ttitle: Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu resources\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu resources\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tExtend the Distributed Workloads queueing layer so that AMD GPU resources\n34\t(amd.com/gpu) are handled in Kueue quota and admission. Today GPU quota\n35\thandling covers NVIDIA resources; AMD Instinct nodes expose amd.com/gpu, and\n36\tjobs requesting them must be admitted with correct quota accounting and gang\n37\tsemantics (all-or-nothing admission via waitForPodsReady).\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Define/configure the Kueue resource flavor and ClusterQueue/LocalQueue\n42\t  quota model for amd.com/gpu resources on AMD Instinct node pools.\n43\t- Ensure admission of multi-pod distributed jobs requesting amd.com/gpu\n44\t  preserves gang semantics (no partial admission of a job's pods).\n45\t- Validate quota accounting and queueing behavior for jobs requesting\n46\t  amd.com/gpu on physical AMD Instinct hardware (hardware access is a shared\n47\t  precondition with the serving validation campaign).\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given a ClusterQueue with an amd.com/gpu flavor, when a workload requests\n52\t  amd.com/gpu resources, then quota is accounted against the flavor and\n53\t  admission respects the configured quota, measured by Kueue workload\n54\t  admission state and quota usage.\n55\t- Given a distributed multi-pod workload requesting amd.com/gpu, when the\n56\t  full request cannot be met, then the workload remains pending without\n57\t  partial pod admission (gang semantics), measured by Kueue admission\n58\t  behavior and pending-workload metrics.\n59\t- Given queues configured for AMD GPU pools, when training workloads are\n60\t  submitted, then they queue and are admitted in order with correct quota\n61\t  handling, measured by Kueue pending/admitted workload metrics.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n66\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n67\t\n68\t## Risks\n69\t\n70\t- Requires physical AMD Instinct hardware for end-to-end validation; access\n71\t  is unresolved at strategy level (procurement or partner lab).\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-843dea58d8e936e4","agent_id":"ac39359585d532d5a","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"414bdf15-4e0b-4ad6-a023-c8823f591bc8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:39:00.359Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af8527b7064ee1ca","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
