daries (no other accelerator families, no\n54\t  AMD GPU sharing/partitioning).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Given the completed AMD GPU enablement work, when the documentation is\n59\t  authored, then it states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and\n60\t  the validated model list, measured by published doc topics covering every\n61\t  item in the content outline.\n62\t- Given the documentation draft, when technically reviewed, then the content\n63\t  is verified against the implemented behavior (runtime images, quota\n64\t  configuration, validated models) by the implementing engineers, measured\n65\t  by a completed technical review sign-off.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver\n70\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-843dea58d8e936e4","agent_id":"ac39359585d532d5a","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"938ef8ae-1e01-4c71-b068-bbd9f0a9cd57","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:39:01.445Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bffbdbfed20260f2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
