{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99b0aec1c1ae8371","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9020\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n9\t  description: 'E003 description says pipeline onboarding starts immediately, but\n10\t    E003 is gated on E001 (dependencies: [RHAISTRAT-9020-E001]) and cannot start until\n11\t    the validation campaign concludes; reword to say onboarding runs parallel to E002\n12\t    after the campaign clears.'\n13\t- severity: minor\n14\t  criterion: Type Correctness\n15\t  description: E002 gate_failure_impact.action is rewrite but the fallback_approach\n16\t    text also covers full no-go removal; the single-action field encodes two outcomes\n17\t    - acceptable, but the remove outcome could be stated more precisely.\n18\terror: null\n19\t---\n20\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9020\n21\t\n22\t## Review Summary\n23\t\n24\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n25\tRecommendation: accept\n26\t\n27\t## Criterion Details\n28\t\n29\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n30\t\n31\tAll four HLRs map to epics with a present traceability matrix: HLR-1 (P0) →\n32\tE001; HLR-2 (P0) → E002, E003; HLR-3 (P1) → E004, E005; HLR-4 (P2) → E006.\n33\tEvery epic's HLR Traceability section matches the summary matrix. Priority\n34\tinheritance is correct: E001 (P0) gates the P0 serving work; E004/E005 are P1\n35\troots enabling only P1 HLR-3 work; E006 (docs-authoring, P1 vs HLR-4's P2)\n36\tcorrectly applies the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority\n37\tMajor → P1), and the deviation is flagged as a health warning. No epic maps to\n38\tHLRs at mixed priority levels, so no priority collapse exists. No triage\n39\tapplied (`triage: null`), so multi-epic output is expected.\n40\t\n41\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n42\t\n43\tDiagram and frontmatter are fully consistent: every edge in the `graph TD`\n44\tdiagram (dependency → dependent) has a matching entry in the target epic's\n45\t`dependencies`, and vice versa (E001→E002, E001→E003, E002→E006, E003→E006,\n46\tE004→E006, E005→E006). No circular dependencies; all referenced epics exist.\n47\t\n48\tRule 10 check: the konflux-onboarding epic (E003) has no blocking edge in\n49\teither direction with the general implementation epic (E002); the only coupling\n50\tis the Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" AC on E002, which is present. E003 → E006\n51\tis a valid Rule 11 edge (docs blocked by all Implementations).\n52\t\n53\tRule 3 check: E002 and E003 both gate on the E001 Investigation with\n54\t`gated_by` recorded and present in `dependencies`, and `gate_failure_impact`\n55\tpopulated (rewrite / remove respectively). Not using conditional branch files\n56\tis correct here: the no-go outcome contains zero epics and the go outcome is\n57\tthe main plan with model-set scope resolved by the gate, so gate metadata is\n58\tthe right encoding — no main-plan epic references a branch node.\n59\t\n60\tRule 13/14 check: E004 ∥ E005 (different repos, no build-against artifact) and\n61\tE004/E005 as roots independent of the serving campaign are justified — HLR-3\n62\tis not gated by the serving-focused HLR-1 campaign. The amd.com/gpu quota\n63\tconfiguration E004's end-to-end AC relies on is a configuration reference\n64\t(test-local quota can stand in), correctly handled as an AC rather than a\n65\t`dependencies` edge.\n66\t\n67\tCritical path length 3 (E001→E002/E003→E006) is appropriate for an M-size,\n68\tfour-component strategy with no new components. Verified against architecture\n69\tcontext: all four strategy components have context files, so no onboarding\n70\tchain (Rule 20 repo-onboarding path) was needed — only the image-build +\n71\tkonflux-onboarding parallel start, which is what the DAG shows.\n72\t\n73\tMinor (non-score-reducing): E003's description says pipeline onboarding\n74\t\"starts immediately and runs in parallel with the runt