m cadence) were correctly NOT typed as\n106\tInvestigations — their answers do not change epic structure, and the\n107\tdispositions are documented in the summary.\n108\t\n109\tMinor (non-score-reducing): E002's `gate_failure_impact.action: rewrite`\n110\tencodes two outcomes in one field — the fallback text covers both a\n111\tpartial-clear scope rewrite and a full no-go removal. Acceptable\n112\tsingle-action encoding, but slightly imprecise.\n113\t\n114\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n115\t\n116\tSignal sets are type-correct: E001 (Investigation) carries\n117\t`investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric) with null `ai_signals`; E002-E006\n118\t(Implementation) carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) with null\n119\t`investigation_signals`. Rationale files exist for all six epics and their\n120\tvalues match frontmatter.\n121\t\n122\tSpot-checks against rubric conditions: E001's `cluster_hardware_dependence:\n123\t-2` is exactly right (the gating question requires AMD Instinct hardware\n124\tpresent in no CI fleet) and `source_accessibility: 0` is right (no readable\n125\tartifact holds the parity answer). E002's `open_questions: -1` and\n126\t`external_dependency: -1` correctly reflect the unresolved campaign scope and\n127\tAMD-controlled image cadence. E003's favorable konflux-onboarding scores\n128\tmatch the \"already-onboarded repos, new variant\" premise confirmed by the\n129\tserving-runtimes architecture context. E006's `human_process_gates: -1`\n130\tcorrectly reflects the mandatory docs technical-review sign-off.\n131\t`ai_implementability` / `ai_implementability_score` are pipeline-computed and\n132\twere not checked per review instructions.\n133\t\n134\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n135\t\n136\tEvery epic has testable Given/When/Then ACs with \"measured by\" clauses.\n137\tRule-mandated ACs are all present: E006 (docs-authoring) has the technical\n138\treview sign-off AC (Rule 24); E002 carries the \"build pipeline green\" AC for\n139