me/ClusterServingRuntime templates that expose the\n51\t  ROCm runtime for AMD Instinct nodes, requesting amd.com/gpu resources.\n52\t- Validate that KServe InferenceServices using the ROCm serving runtime\n53\t  schedule and serve correctly on AMD Instinct nodes (KServe itself requires\n54\t  no code changes — this is the passive-component validation).\n55\t- Ensure the build pipeline for the ROCm image variant is green through the\n56\t  onboarded Konflux setup (the pipeline onboarding runs in parallel; its\n57\t  first green execution gates release, not development).\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given the cleared-model list from the validation campaign, when the ROCm\n62\t  serving runtime is productized, then every cleared model serves\n63\t  successfully on AMD Instinct nodes via KServe InferenceServices, measured\n64\t  by end-to-end serving tests per cleared model.\n65\t- Given the ROCm runtime image, when it is released, then the image digest is\n66\t  pinned to an upstream ROCm release compatible with the platform release\n67\t  train, measured by the release manifest.\n68\t- Given an InferenceService selecting the ROCm serving runtime, when deployed\n69\t  to a node pool with AMD Instinct accelerators, then pods schedule with\n70\t  amd.com/gpu resources and become Ready, measured by InferenceService status\n71\t  conditions.\n72\t- Given the Konflux build pipeline for the ROCm image variant, when a change\n73\t  lands, then the pipeline builds the image green, measured by a passing\n74\t  Konflux build for the runtime image.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n79\t  models the validation campaign clears.\n80\t\n81\t## Risks\n82\t\n83\t- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n84\t  communities and may not align with platform release trains.\n85\t- Full no-go from the validation campaign removes this epic; a partial\n86\t  cleared-model list rewrites its scope.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f590fb60777572e","agent_id":"a913619b5c3699182","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"0161be51-c94a-4a66-90d4-bd6b371b70ec","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:43:22.026Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-accb8dfe513a20ef","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
