{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82b129bfe417a102","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: On a partial clear, scope is rewritten to the exact model subset\n15\t    the validation campaign clears. On a full no-go (zero models clear), this epic\n16\t    is removed outright and no vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tProductize a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models cleared by\n39\tthe AMD Instinct validation campaign, so that RHOAI can serve those models on\n40\tAMD accelerators. Today only CUDA (NVIDIA) runtime builds are productized;\n41\tupstream vLLM publishes ROCm builds that are not shipped or supported. This\n42\tepic turns the validated subset into a productized runtime.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Build and release a vLLM ROCm serving runtime image from the existing\n47\t  midstream vLLM repos, for the model set cleared by the validation campaign.\n48\t- Pin the image to an upstream ROCm runtime release aligned with the platform\n49\t  release train (upstream cadence is AMD/community-controlled; tracking and\n50\t  digest pinning is part of this scope).\n51\t- Provide the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime templates that expose the\n52\t  ROCm runtime for AMD Instinct nodes, requesting amd.com/gpu resources.\n53\t- Validate that KServe InferenceServices using the ROCm serving runtime\n54\t  schedule and serve correctly on AMD Instinct nodes (KServe itself requires\n55\t  no code changes — this is the passive-component validation).\n56\t- Ensure the build pipeline for the ROCm image variant is green through the\n57\t  onboarded Konflux setup (the pipeline onboarding runs in parallel; its\n58\t  first green execution gates release, not development).\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- Given the cleared-model list from the validation campaign, when the ROCm\n63\t  serving runtime is productized, then every cleared model serves\n64\t  successfully on AMD Instinct nodes via KServe InferenceServices, measured\n65\t  by end-to-end serving tests per cleared model.\n66\t- Given the ROCm runtime image, when it is released, then the image digest is\n67\t  pinned to an upstream ROCm release compatible with the platform release\n68\t  train, measured by the release manifest.\n69\t- Given an InferenceService selecting the ROCm serving runtime, when deployed\n70\t  to a node pool with AMD Instinct accelerators, then pods schedule with\n71\t  amd.com/gpu resources and become Ready, measured by InferenceService status\n72\t  conditions.\n73\t- Given the Konflux build pipeline for the ROCm image variant, when a change\n74\t  lands, then the pipeline builds the image green, measured by a passing\n75\t  Konflux build for the runtime image.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n80\t  models the validation campaign clears.\n81\t\n82\t## Risks\n83\t\n84\t- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n85\t  communities and may not align with platform release trains.\n86\t- Full no-go from the validation campaign removes this epic; a partial\n87\t  cleared-model list rewrites its scope.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaa2c4ed914d3629","agent_id":"af547be916899f51a","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"60861d6c-cc17-476a-a3da-ed75b144a550","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:45:43.686Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82b129bfe417a102","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae18cfe93eb0361f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: Konflux build pipeline for the vLLM ROCm serving image\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: konflux-onboarding\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the validation campaign no-goes, no ROCm image is productized\n16\t    and the dedicated build pipeline is not needed.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\tinvestigation_signals: null\n28\tai_implementability: High\n29\tai_implementability_score: 6\n30\tjira_key: null\n31\tbranch: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Konflux build pipeline for the vLLM ROCm serving image\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tOnboard the build pipeline for the new vLLM ROCm serving runtime image\n38\tvariant into Konflux. The vLLM midstream repos are already Konflux-onboarded\n39\tfor existing (CUDA) builds; this epic adds the build configuration for the\n40\tROCm image variant so it can be built and released through the standard\n41\tplatform pipeline. This is a new container image in an existing repo, so no\n42\trepo onboarding is needed — once the validation campaign concludes with a go\n43\tdecision, pipeline onboarding starts and runs in parallel with the runtime\n44\timage implementation work (there is no serial repo-onboarding chain; the only\n45\tupstream gate is the campaign itself).\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Add Konflux build configuration (image variant, build recipe) for the vLLM\n50\t  ROCm serving runtime image in the existing onboarded repos.\n51\t- Wire the new image variant into the existing release pipeline so it is\n52\t  built and published per platform version alongside the CUDA builds.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given the Konflux configuration for the ROCm image variant, when a build\n57\t  is triggered, then the image builds green through Konflux, measured by a\n58\t  passing pipeline run producing the ROCm runtime image.\n59\t- Given the release pipeline, when a platform version is cut, then the ROCm\n60\t  image variant is built and published through the same mechanism as the\n61\t  existing runtime builds, measured by the released image artifact.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n66\t  models the validation campaign clears (build-pipeline enablement).\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaa2c4ed914d3629","agent_id":"af547be916899f51a","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"57d9e825-c94e-4077-b4d4-9fd77d4c3c5c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:45:43.688Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae18cfe93eb0361f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
