{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b4d71ee4484816a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support for Training Operator jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: -1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support for Training Operator jobs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tEnable PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) for single- and\n34\tmulti-GPU jobs run through the Training Operator's PyTorchJob resource.\n35\tUpstream PyTorch publishes ROCm support; this epic brings that support to the\n36\tplatform's training path so data scientists can train on AMD GPUs with the\n37\tsame job APIs used for NVIDIA GPUs today.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Provide PyTorch ROCm worker images (or approved image references) usable by\n42\t  PyTorchJob pods on AMD Instinct nodes, pinned to upstream ROCm releases.\n43\t- Ensure PyTorchJob specs can request amd.com/gpu resources for both\n44\t  single-GPU and multi-GPU (distributed) job topologies.\n45\t- Validate functional training on physical AMD Instinct hardware (hardware\n46\t  access is a shared precondition with the serving validation campaign).\n47\t- Validate end-to-end admission and execution of multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n48\t  through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota (the quota configuration itself is\n49\t  tracked separately by the Distributed Workloads component; this epic\n50\t  verifies jobs flow through it).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given a PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu resources, when submitted to a\n55\t  cluster with AMD Instinct nodes, then the job runs training to completion\n56\t  on ROCm, measured by successful job completion status for single-GPU and\n57\t  multi-GPU topologies.\n58\t- Given a multi-GPU PyTorchJob on ROCm, when submitted through a Kueue-backed\n59\t  queue with amd.com/gpu quota configured, then the job is admitted and all\n60\t  pods run, measured by Kueue admission state and job completion.\n61\t- Given the PyTorch ROCm worker images, when used per documentation, then the\n62\t  pinned image references are recorded for release, measured by the release\n63\t  manifest.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n68\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n69\t\n70\t## Risks\n71\t\n72\t- Requires physical AMD Instinct hardware for validation; access is\n73\t  unresolved at strategy level (procurement or partner lab).\n74\t- Upstream PyTorch/ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and upstream\n75\t  communities.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaa2c4ed914d3629","agent_id":"af547be916899f51a","session_id":"b78dd159-7f4d-4694-995d-eb214297feef","uuid":"ef5b69e7-d6d8-48a0-9951-76bc775fb255","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:45:47.377Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b4d71ee4484816a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
